  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 151 PM EDT Tue May 12 2026\n\nOvernight lows Thursday into Friday will give us a final taste of \nchill air before Summer returns. Lows Friday morning could fall into \nthe mid to upper 40s for most of the CWA. Temps will begin to climb \non Friday back into the mid to upper 80s. As the ridge continues to \nbuild the main concern in the forecast will be this weekends heat. \n90 degree temperatures are expected this weekend, though the dry air \nwill limit the potential for dangerous heat indices. \n\nDry conditions may bring back some fire weather concerns, though \nmost of the state has received enough rain to reduce some of the \nrisk that we were facing a few weeks back. Regardless, please \ncontinue to monitor the Fire Weather Forecast as we approach the \nmiddle of the week for potential critical fire weather.",
